      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "Moses starts by speaking to the children of Israel in the wilderness, addressing those things they came out of. It’s good to note that much of who he is talking to now (aside from Joshua and Caleb) is a completely new generation. The generation that left Egypt has all passed away at this point, and their children are the only ones left to remain. The reason for this being that they were completely reliant on their own strength and not on God’s. Moses will be giving an account of what their fathers had to go through just to get to this point.",
