      "id": "deuteronomy_1_9_deuteronomy-1-9-18_19",
      "book": "Deuteronomy",
      "chapter": 1,
      "verse": 9,
      "startVerse": 9,
      "endVerse": 16,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "The great issue with every leader is the struggle of conflict and drama from those he’s leading. Leaders tend to listen to the negative reviews more than the positive ones (even if there are more positive than negative). Furthermore, most leaders feel the burden to shoulder all of the responsibilities that God has placed on them alone. In fact, most leaders don’t feel like they have the ability to trust someone else with their burdens, which causes a heavy heart and a bad spirit if it’s not put into check.",
